theorem a-power-said-not-zero
  note        A quotient's divisor not being zero is the step's to write, a power to a letter among them, where the page does not say once it is a positive integer.
  let n ∈ ℕ    (H1)
  let ε ∈ ℝ    (H2)
  let x ∈ ℝ    (H3)
  assume x^n > 0    (H4)
  assume 1/x^n < ε    (H5)
  then 1 − ε < 1 − 1/x^n

1.  1 − ε < 1 − 1/x^n
    inequalities
      1/x^n < ε              H5
      −1/x^n > −ε            multiplying by −1
      1 − 1/x^n > 1 − ε      adding 1
    requires x^n ≠ 0: weakening, from H4
